==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[œconomist]] {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|économiste||lang=frm|household manager}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[expert]] in [[economics]], especially one who studies [[economic]] data and extracts higher-level [[information]] or proposes [[theories]].
# One concerned with [[political economy]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} One who [[manages]] a [[household]].
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} One who economizes, or manages domestic or other concerns with frugality; one who expends money, time, or labor, judiciously, and without waste.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|one who economizes}} [[economiser]], [[economizer]], [[miser]]

====Related terms====
* [[economy]]

